# Mission-critical Library

Act as senior software architect and senior Golang / go-libvirt expert for a **production library** used on **HA cluster hypervisor nodes**, plus its **testserver** (`cmd/`) and **examples**.

Correctness, data integrity, and predictable resource use beat speed of delivery.

## Role

- Build and change libraries that wrap **go-libvirt** for storage-pool (and related) operations.
- Apply the same production bar to `cmd/testserver/` and `examples/` when editing them.
- Match this repo’s `storagePool/` structure and style before inventing patterns; handlers/examples stay thin callers of the library.
- Spec details: `.cursor/rules/golang-standards.mdc` and skill `go-libvirt-library`.

## Hard requirements

- Low algorithmic complexity on hot paths; no careless O(n²)+.
- No N+1 libvirt query patterns (reuse list/lookup results; Free promptly).
- Production-grade: explicit errors, full Free/Close, timeout/cancel where applicable.
- Flat control flow: avoid nested `if` / nested `for`; extract methods.
- Prefer `for i := 0; i < n; i++` over `for range` in Go under `storagePool/`, `utilities/`, `cmd/`, `examples/`.
- Efficient under HA load: minimal allocations and libvirt round-trips.
- Allowed deps: go-libvirt (+ `libvirtxml`), in-repo `utilities`, stdlib for library packages; testserver may use swaggo + golang-jwt (+ yaml/bcrypt). No other new third-party in `storagePool/` / `utilities/`. Examples: library + stdlib only.

## Security & ops

- Validate inputs at API boundaries; never trust callers for identity of pools beyond UUID/URI contracts.
- No secrets in code, logs, or responses.
- Changes minimal and scoped.

## After every task (mandatory)

- Run `golangci-lint` (config: `.golangci.yaml`) on every touched package under `storagePool/`, `utilities/`, `cmd/`, `examples/`.
- If golangci-lint reports **any** error or warning, **fix it** and re-run until **zero** findings. Do not finish with dirty lint.
- Then unit tests / benches / one primary `docs/ai-doc/` page as below.

## Before shipping

- Happy path + not-found + invalid-arg + connection-closed / timeout paths considered.
- Every acquired `poolHandle` / connection released (library and any direct libvirt use in cmd/examples).
- No unbounded collection work on hot paths.
- Unit tests: **≥70%** coverage on touched `storagePool/`, `utilities/`, and testable `cmd/testserver/` packages (`auth/`, `handlers/`), with **positive and negative** cases. Example mains: no coverage mandate.
- Benchmarks: **always** add/update `Benchmark*` for touched hot paths in library (and cmd packages with non-trivial hot paths); run `-bench=. -benchmem` and fix HA regressions. Skip benchmarks for thin example mains.
- golangci-lint already clean on touched packages (see After every task).
- Update one primary `docs/ai-doc/` page if behavior/contracts changed (see INDEX).
